WEBVTT

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:03.610
Pongal's skill, Counterblast!

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:06.250
I add Soul Saver Dragon to my hand!

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.810
I'm ready.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:14.410
Mr. Mitsusada, I'm gonna charge 
at you with everything I've got!

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.370
Just like I thought!

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:01.270
I attack Enigman Wave with 
Knight of Friendship, Kay!

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:05.480
When Kay attacks, he receives +3000 power!

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:08.000
I guard with Enigman Ripple!

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:15.980
With a boost from Marron, 
Blaster Blade attacks!

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:19.450
No guard!

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:21.150
Drive check!

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:28.040
Damage check!

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:31.230
With a boost from Wingal Brave...

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:34.140
...Knight of Loyalty, Bedivere attacks!

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:38.960
My Vanguard is Blaster Blade, so 
Bedivere receives another +3000!

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.390
I guard with Guide Dolphin!

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:47.020
My turn ends.

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:51.130
All I could do was 1 damage.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:54.600
But... I'm prepared for my next attack.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.500
That 1 damage was from Soul Saver Dragon...

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:04.290
And he's set up his next 
turn's attack already.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:09.140
Aichi, you're a fitting rival for me.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:18.540
But that being the case, I'll 
go all out to crush your plan.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:23.580
The Man They Call "The Emperor"

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.750
Stand and draw!

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.060
Summon your courage, my 
invincible superhuman!

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:34.390
I ride Enigman Storm!

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:39.700
And then I call...

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:46.000
With a boost from Cosmo Roar...

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.950
...Masked Police, Grander attacks 
Knight of Loyalty, Bedivere!

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:52.420
My rear-guard?!

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:54.600
Grander's skill!

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.110
My Vanguard receives +2000 power!

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.440
With a boost from Guide Dolphin...

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.450
...Enigman Shine attacks 
Knight of Friendship, Kay!

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.270
I see...

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:20.180
Mr. Mitsusada is trying to destroy 
my Soul Saver Dragon strategy...

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.100
Soul Saver Dragon's skill...

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.830
With a five-card Soulblast,

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:29.000
you can give power to up to 
three of your rear-guards,

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.640
thereby increasing your 
entire attacking power.

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:35.620
But if I decrease the number 
of units in your rear-guard...

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:37.880
...I can weaken the power of that attack.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:41.200
The Emperor really is strong!

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:49.000
You did a nice job of preparing this 
attack during the previous turn...

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:52.630
...but I won't let you use it freely.

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:01.340
The fight is going in Mitsusada's direction.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:08.520
Once a fight is going in one direction, 
it's extremely difficult to turn it around.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.830
Sendou is out of Mitsusada's league.

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:14.410
The direction of the fight can't be changed.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:17.270
There's only one way the tide could turn.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:20.760
He has to rely on his power.

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:30.290
So... use it.

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.950
Become hooked on the power again...

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:39.330
Then subdue Mitsusada and humiliate him!

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.760
Show me the victory that I'm craving...

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:44.060
...Aichi!

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:49.480
Enigman Storm attacks Blaster Blade!

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:55.390
Twin drive check.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:58.620
Stand trigger.

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:00.640
Enigman Shine stands.

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:02.470
I add +5000 to his power.

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:11.580
Damage check!

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:14.090
Enigman Shine!

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:29.700
That's the end of my turn.

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:35.290
Mr. Mitsusada really is 
an incredible fighter.

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:38.220
He figured I was going to use 
Soul Saver Dragon's skill...

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:42.230
...so he weakened its potential 
effect while dealing 2 damage.

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:45.400
This is a top-level fighter.

00:06:47.980 --> 00:06:51.010
Am I a match for him?

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:53.760
What should I do?

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:05.730
Wait!

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:10.600
The power of Psyqualia...

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:16.010
...shows me you guys and the future of 
Cardfights. I'm not turning down this power!

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:16.750
But...

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:19.990
...without my own strength,

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:25.480
I'll surely become addicted 
to the power again.

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:31.710
That's why I'm not going 
to rely on the power today!

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:35.110
I want to fight Mr. Mitsusada...

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:38.110
...using my own strength!

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:41.240
Give everything I've got 
to compete with him...

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:44.490
...to become stronger myself!

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:50.960
What's this?

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:58.990
For just a moment, I sensed Psyqualia...

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:00.180
...but it disappeared?

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:02.860
What does that mean?

00:08:04.070 --> 00:08:05.090
Draw!

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:10.180
Sacred dragon! Appear and 
muster your mystical power!

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:13.270
I ride Soul Saver Dragon!

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.800
I Soulblast five cards!

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:28.520
Holy Charging Roar!

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:36.630
Normally, I would have been able to 
power up three units with this skill...

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:42.180
Still, even with limited power, I'm not done 
until I've fought with all of its might!

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:43.070
I call...

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:46.280
Swordsman of the Explosive Flames, Palamedes!

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:48.290
Attack Enigman Storm!

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:52.000
Intercept!

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:53.440
Grander!

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:57.780
With a boost from Marron...

00:08:58.250 --> 00:09:00.400
...Soul Saver Dragon attacks!

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:04.470
No guard.

00:09:04.970 --> 00:09:06.420
Twin drive check.

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:19.300
Damage check.

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:21.550
With a boost from Wingal Brave...

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:23.470
...Gordon attacks!

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:26.360
I guard with Cosmo Fang!

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:37.010
That's the end of my turn.

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:39.140
Shoot!

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:44.550
If Soul Saver Dragon's skill had worked to full 
capacity, he would've done 1 more point of damage!

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:49.610
Well, Aichi, because I 
consider you my rival...

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:52.590
...I'm going to challenge 
you by going all out!

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:55.460
I put Guide Dolphin into the Soul...

00:09:55.890 --> 00:09:58.530
...so I can add +3000 to 
the power of Enigman Storm!

00:09:59.510 --> 00:10:01.190
I call Cosmo Beak!

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:02.890
Counterblast!

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:06.600
I add +4000 to the power of 
Enigman Storm. And then...

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:07.880
...I call...

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:12.300
Enigman Storm's skill!

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:16.240
If his power is 15000 or more, 
he gets an extra critical!

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:20.420
An extra critical?!

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:24.520
With that position, the Emperor's 
battle formation is decided.

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:25.730
He's playing seriously...

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:29.960
Nobody would be able to 
withstand his next attack.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:34.400
Just like no one would be able to 
successfully resist the Roman emperor.

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:37.620
With a boost from Glory Maker...

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:40.390
...Enigman Storm attacks Gordon!

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:42.150
Gordon?!

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:45.250
I'm going to keep you from intercepting.

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:48.770
You see, I really want my attack 
against your Vanguard to succeed!

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:51.210
Glory Maker's skill!

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.930
When she boosts, if there's 
4 or more damage...

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:56.270
...my Vanguard receives +4000 power!

00:10:56.810 --> 00:10:58.300
He's got 28000 power!

00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:59.540
G2P!

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:01.850
But doesn't it seem like kind of a waste?

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:05.820
If he's got that much power, why would 
he use it against the rear-guard?

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:06.530
Good question...

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:09.470
Rear-guards should fight rear-guards!

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:10.890
I don't think so.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:13.490
Well, you'll see.

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:16.260
Twin drive check!

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:17.270
First card...

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:19.930
Second card...

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:23.720
A trigger couldn't have 
come at a better time.

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:25.790
Stand trigger activated!

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:28.670
I add +5000 to the power of Enigman Storm!

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:31.110
And then Glory Maker stands!

00:11:42.290 --> 00:11:45.260
Now, I'll show you great power!

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:47.830
Commander Laurel's skill!

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:49.990
Four of my rear-guard units rest!

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:55.100
And then... stand, Enigman Storm!

00:11:55.710 --> 00:11:57.330
One more time with Storm?!

00:11:57.700 --> 00:12:01.780
This is my special weapon, 
"Dictator's Final Domination"!

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:26.460
I see. Commander Laurel's skill 
lets the Vanguard stand up.

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:29.350
So then he attacks with Storm...

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:32.080
STHAWSNP?

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:33.780
With "no problem", you say?

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:40.470
And since the cost for activating that 
skill is "resting four rear-guard units",

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:43.510
it's not like he could use any of them first.

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:49.590
This was the best way to go about 
destroying the interceptors...

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:52.220
...in order to make his attack 
on the Vanguard a sure thing.

00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:55.340
And we can't forget about...

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:57.260
...Enigman Storm's...

00:12:58.370 --> 00:12:59.770
The extra critical!

00:13:01.490 --> 00:13:03.780
Aichi already has 4 damage.

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:06.180
If he takes 2 damage now...

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:09.920
And he made Glory Maker 
stand with a trigger, too...

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:12.920
Yes. So his attack's going 
to be at full power!

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:16.280
That'll make Soul Saver Dragon explode!

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:18.480
This doesn't look good, Brother...

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:21.350
The third match of the semifinal!

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:26.050
Sendou of Team Q4 is approaching 
his direst moment...

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:27.430
My heart is pounding!

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:32.670
My battle with you is going to end here.

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:35.450
I'll go easy on you by making it quick.

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:37.740
I won't prolong the agony.

00:13:39.640 --> 00:13:40.740
Why?

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:48.400
He's in an overwhelmingly 
unfavorable situation...

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:50.140
...so how can he look so calm?

00:13:53.570 --> 00:13:56.510
That's Aichi's true strength!

00:13:57.820 --> 00:13:59.610
Huh...!

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:01.370
That kid's pretty impressive...

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:05.520
Uh huh. That may be his true strength.

00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:09.160
We didn't see it until now 
because he was using Psyqualia.

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:11.280
He reminds me of...

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:15.060
Yeah. That last time, when 
Brother battled him...

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:25.900
Glory Maker's boost!

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:28.020
Go, Enigman Storm!

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:31.050
With Glory Maker's skill, the total is 33000!

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:37.340
I'm not giving up.

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:40.060
Everyone, please help!

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:46.300
Twin drive check!

00:14:56.470 --> 00:15:01.670
Wonderful! You left yourself enough 
power to protect against this attack!

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:04.970
If you're going to come at me with 
all your might, Mr. Mitsusada,

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:07.180
I'll defend with all <i>my</i> strength!

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:09.090
Awesome...

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:12.510
They're both using all of their 
power against each other!

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:13.480
Indeed.

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:15.890
A fight with two hearts in tune...

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:19.500
That's much more valuable than...

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:21.680
...bringing your opponent to his knees.

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:28.770
Ren?

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:34.030
My turn ends.

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:37.710
I'm impressed you blocked that attack. But...

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:41.300
I know. You're a great 
fighter, Mr. Mitsusada.

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:43.240
Your attack just now made me...

00:15:46.430 --> 00:15:49.550
Aichi saved himself from taking 
any damage this turn...

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.800
...but he doesn't have any 
cards left in his hand.

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:53.830
And he's down a unit in the front row.

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:58.410
It's a shame! It's his turn to attack, 
but he's running out of allies!

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:00.520
Mitsusada, on the other hand...

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:08.100
Two of those cards in his hand are 
perfect defense cards, Diamond Ace!

00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:10.710
They can totally protect up to two attacks!

00:16:10.710 --> 00:16:14.450
Making matters worse, in the front row 
is a Cosmo Beak, which can intercept.

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:20.690
Even though it's my turn, 
I'm in a bad position.

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:25.920
But I've done everything I can so far.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:29.110
All that's left are me and my allies...

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:32.320
I'll fight with all I've got!

00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:38.590
You... you came for me?

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:43.800
See the king in his younger days

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:46.020
as he blazes a trail with his knights!

00:16:46.580 --> 00:16:47.430
What?!

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:50.240
I ride...

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:53.290
...Alfred Early!

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:01.530
<i>Now</i> he gets Alfred Early?

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:03.910
He can do it! He still has 
a chance with that card!

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:06.410
Alfred Early's skill!

00:17:06.410 --> 00:17:08.920
Stand up again, my avatar!

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.250
Superior call, Blaster Blade!

00:17:13.310 --> 00:17:16.900
With Blaster Blade's skill, 
Cosmo Beak exits the field!

00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:18.670
Counterblast!

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.650
I've stopped your intercept.

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:31.940
Now we can get an attack through!

00:17:32.100 --> 00:17:36.050
Sendou wants to make the most of this chance!

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:39.200
And what great timing with Alfred Early!

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:44.440
<i>Oh</i>, yes, indeed! It's as if the unit 
itself came to help him of its own will!

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:46.130
Will, he says...

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:48.900
That boy did say "we", didn't he?

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:51.650
Even though he's not using Psyqualia...

00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:53.440
That's right.

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:56.770
That kind of thing can happen, you know?

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:00.300
Although I'm sure you haven't 
had any experiences like that...

00:18:01.190 --> 00:18:05.650
When a fighter does their best, their 
allies won't leave them in the lurch.

00:18:06.530 --> 00:18:08.810
The units have their own will...

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:11.010
There are moments where you sense that.

00:18:14.890 --> 00:18:17.510
I attack with Swordsman of 
the Explosive Flames, Palamedes!

00:18:25.740 --> 00:18:27.430
5 damage...

00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:29.670
But I'll protect myself against 
your remaining attacks!

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:31.950
With a boost from Marron...

00:18:32.260 --> 00:18:34.370
...Alfred Early attacks!

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:40.620
Perfect guard with Diamond Ace!

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:48.730
Twin drive...

00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:50.310
First check!

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:53.590
Second check...

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:58.620
Sharon!

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:01.470
Thank you for coming!

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:06.360
Stand trigger! I add +5000 to 
the power of Blaster Blade!

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:08.650
And then Palamedes stands!

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:19.780
Thanks to that stand trigger, it's 
possible for him to attack twice more...

00:19:20.710 --> 00:19:23.300
I've got one more perfect guard...

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:28.410
Even if I block his next attack, I 
can't block the next one after it...

00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:30.700
Here I go!

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:33.340
With a boost from Wingal Brave...

00:19:33.340 --> 00:19:35.330
...Blaster Blade attacks!

00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:36.550
In that case...

00:19:36.550 --> 00:19:37.370
...no guard!

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:42.320
I leave what happens to the judgment 
of fate known as triggers!

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:55.720
Damage check!

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:03.430
Too bad. This is as far as I go.

00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:05.990
The winner...

00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:08.160
...Aichi Sendou!

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:12.110
He did it!

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:13.420
Yes!

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:17.180
The teams advancing to the final 
round have been decided at last!

00:20:17.180 --> 00:20:22.320
Team AL4 and Team Q4! These 
teams will clash tomorrow!

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:23.930
I'm s-<i>o</i> excited!

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:26.430
Amazing!

00:20:27.170 --> 00:20:30.210
To think he won without using Psyqualia...

00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:32.950
But he can't afford to do that tomorrow.

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:35.740
Not if Ren Suzugamori is his opponent...

00:20:35.740 --> 00:20:39.270
A battle between two people 
with the power of Psyqualia...

00:20:39.270 --> 00:20:41.420
Will the winner be the "chosen one"?

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:43.300
Instead of focusing on who will win,

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:47.900
I think it means enough that 
they're going to fight.

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:50.790
And when they do, Psyqualia's...

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:52.910
...true meaning will be revealed.

00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:55.660
Is that the will of you-know-who?

00:21:05.310 --> 00:21:10.000
Brother! I-I'm kind of moved!

00:21:10.350 --> 00:21:14.930
I know we can trust you guys 
with the job of taking down AL4.

00:21:14.930 --> 00:21:17.290
Get 'em for us, too!

00:21:20.620 --> 00:21:23.490
I'm sure it'll be okay! Just do your best!

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:24.980
Right!

00:21:24.980 --> 00:21:26.510
Hey!

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:29.130
Tomorrow's the final round!

00:21:29.130 --> 00:21:31.640
Let's go home so we can all rest up!

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:33.190
Roger!

00:21:33.190 --> 00:21:34.150
See ya!

00:21:38.300 --> 00:21:39.230
Final
Team FFAL4 vs Team Q4

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:40.200
Championship
Final

00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:46.030
So our opponents are Q4.

00:21:46.670 --> 00:21:50.910
Do you really think you can 
beat me fighting like that...

00:21:50.930 --> 00:21:52.160
...Aichi?

00:21:55.720 --> 00:21:58.220
You can keep that face right now...

00:21:58.220 --> 00:21:59.390
but tomorrow...

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:04.680
The gate to hell is already open before all of you.

00:23:51.670 --> 00:23:54.100
Aichi, that was a great fight!

00:23:54.100 --> 00:23:57.670
Have faith in your teammates, and defy AL4!

00:23:57.670 --> 00:23:58.010
Right!

00:23:58.340 --> 00:24:00.250
I was able to make it this far...

00:24:00.250 --> 00:24:01.980
...because of Kamui, Misaki...

00:24:01.980 --> 00:24:03.230
and Kai!

00:24:03.720 --> 00:24:06.110
Next time: Fateful Showdown!

00:24:06.110 --> 00:24:08.200
Ren's Psyqualia is really powerful!

00:24:08.510 --> 00:24:11.060
His opponent will be swallowed 
up by an image of isolation.

00:24:11.180 --> 00:24:14.970
Ren, your power doesn't scare me anymore.

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:17.130
I'm going to bring back the 
person you used to be!

00:24:17.130 --> 00:24:18.120
Kai...
